---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import family from '../images/mau-family.webp';
---

<Base
  title="About Will Mau | Schalmont School Board, Mauops Founder"
  description="The longer story of Will Mau (William Mau) of Rotterdam, New York. Schalmont CSD Board of Education member, VP of Operations at TalentSmartEQ, Scouting committee chair, Mauops founder."
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <SiteHeader />
      <div class="wrap page-hero__inner">
        <p class="kicker page-hero__kicker" data-reveal>About</p>
        <h1 class="page-hero__title" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
          The longer<br />story.
        </h1>
        <p class="page-hero__note" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
          How I got here, what I actually do, and the people who decide
          whether any of it matters.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="essay">
      <div class="wrap essay__wrap">
        <div class="essay__col">
          <p class="essay__lede" data-reveal>
            Three years ago I started showing up to Schalmont board meetings
            because my daughter&rsquo;s kindergarten class was too big.
          </p>

          <p data-reveal>
            I was not planning to run for anything. I just wanted to understand
            the problem and see if it could be fixed. It could. Parents talked,
            we worked with the administration, and we got an additional section
            added the next school year. More importantly, the teachers got
            more support.
          </p>

          <p data-reveal>
            That experience taught me something I had not expected, which is
            that most things in civic life are like that. The system is not
            broken so much as it is quiet, waiting for someone to pay
            attention, ask questions, and follow through. So a year later I
            ran for the board. I have spent the last two years doing exactly
            that, and in May 2026 voters reelected me to a second term.
          </p>

          <figure class="essay__photo" data-reveal>
            <Image
              src={family}
              alt="Will Mau at home in Rotterdam with his wife and two children."
              widths={[480, 720, 960]}
              sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 720px"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Home in Rotterdam with my wife and kids.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <h2 class="essay__h2" data-reveal>What I actually do</h2>

          <p data-reveal>
            My day job is Vice President of Operations at TalentSmartEQ, where
            I sit on a four-person Executive Leadership Team and run operations
            and technology for a remote-first emotional-intelligence training
            company. The work is heavy on Salesforce, AI agents, and the
            unglamorous infrastructure that keeps a company running. I like
            that work.
          </p>

          <p data-reveal>
            On the side, I run
            <a href="https://mauops.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mauops</a>,
            a solo Salesforce, AI, and automation consultancy for small
            businesses. The same diagnosis works almost everywhere: most
            companies pay for software they barely use and do by hand the
            things that should be automated. There is no shortage of work.
          </p>

          <p data-reveal>
            Outside of work, I chair the committee for Troop 3054, the local
            Scout troop based in Schenectady. I serve on the Schalmont
            Central School District Board of Education. My wife is a third
            grade teacher. We have two kids in the district, both Schalmont
            students.
          </p>

          <h2 class="essay__h2" data-reveal>What ties it together</h2>

          <p data-reveal>
            If anything ties all of this together, it is the same instinct
            that pulled me into that first board meeting. Notice the thing.
            Ask the question. Build the system that keeps it from breaking
            again next year. Then move on to the next thing.
          </p>

          <p data-reveal>
            If you want the formal version, the
            <a href="/resume">r&eacute;sum&eacute;</a> is here. If you want to
            reach me, I am at
            <a href="mailto:William.Mau@gmail.com">William.Mau@gmail.com</a>
            or
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/will-mau/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">on LinkedIn</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .essay {
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 4rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem);
  }
  .essay__wrap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .essay__col {
    max-width: 36rem;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .essay__col p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1rem + 0.3vw, 1.18rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .essay__lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 1.1rem + 0.7vw, 1.55rem) !important;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 2rem !important;
  }
  .essay__col a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--green-deep);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: color 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease;
  }
  .essay__col a:hover {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }
  .essay__h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1.2rem + 0.6vw, 1.7rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 2.6rem 0 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .essay__photo {
    margin: 2.6rem -2rem 2.6rem;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .essay__photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .essay__photo figcaption {
    margin: 0.75rem 0.25rem 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .essay__photo { margin: 2rem 0; }
  }
</style>
